1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,974
Namaste — this is Liam, in for Bear. In
May, Bear published an argument about

2
00:00:03,974 --> 00:00:07,999
phones, school technology, and where the
money should actually go. Then he did

3
00:00:07,999 --> 00:00:12,076
something most people who publish an
argument never do. He had it attacked. Not

4
00:00:12,076 --> 00:00:16,411
reviewed. Attacked — under instructions to
fix or kill every number in it. This film

5
00:00:16,411 --> 00:00:17,340
is what came back.

6
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:21,533
Here is the whole film in one breath. The
essay says the binding constraint on

7
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:25,358
technology in schools is teacher
capability — not the device policy, not

8
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:29,395
the platform. The audit says that
recommendation is defensible. It also says

9
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:33,538
four of the sentences carrying it are
wrong, and the study that would actually

10
00:00:33,538 --> 00:00:35,450
prove it has not been run by anyone.

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,963
Start with the argument as published,
because the audit only means something if

12
00:00:39,963 --> 00:00:42,110
you take the argument seriously first.

13
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:46,266
The policy debate offered two answers to
one question. Technology is harming

14
00:00:46,266 --> 00:00:50,425
students — what do we do? Answer one: ban
the phone. Answer two: buy a better

15
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,640
platform. Both answers arrive with force.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:56,692
Neither of them reaches the classroom,
because neither of them is about the

17
00:00:56,692 --> 00:00:57,880
person standing in it.

18
00:00:57,930 --> 00:01:02,332
The best causal evidence on bans comes
from one large Florida district. And it

19
00:01:02,332 --> 00:01:06,564
found something uncomfortable. The
disciplinary cost lands in year one. The

20
00:01:06,564 --> 00:01:11,079
academic benefit shows up in year two. For
a student suspended out of a critical

21
00:01:11,079 --> 00:01:13,280
semester, later is not the same as yes.

22
00:01:13,330 --> 00:01:17,351
Then the essay finds a blank. Phone-ban
statutes carve out an exemption for

23
00:01:17,351 --> 00:01:21,479
educational purposes. The teacher is
handed the judgement — in the moment, at

24
00:01:21,479 --> 00:01:23,731
nine in the morning, with a room watching.

25
00:01:23,731 --> 00:01:28,180
The essay's charge is that the laws hand
over the decision without handing over the

26
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:28,770
definition.

27
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:30,850
So the essay asks for three things.

28
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:35,663
Supervised technology time that replaces
what the ban removed. A definition written

29
00:01:35,663 --> 00:01:39,897
before the rule is enforced. And
sustained, subject-specific training for

30
00:01:39,897 --> 00:01:44,652
teachers in how AI changes what teaching
requires. That is the claim. Now watch it

31
00:01:44,652 --> 00:01:45,580
get taken apart.

32
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:50,080
The audit did not argue with the
conclusion. It went after the sentences.

33
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:54,549
First it refused to rule on the argument
as a whole. It cut the claim into seven

34
00:01:54,549 --> 00:01:56,814
pieces and ruled on each one separately —

35
00:01:56,814 --> 00:02:01,399
because an argument that is sixty percent
right is not sixty percent true. It has a

36
00:02:01,399 --> 00:02:04,990
specific list of parts that hold and a
specific list that do not.

37
00:02:05,040 --> 00:02:07,267
Start with the number the essay opened on.

38
00:02:07,267 --> 00:02:11,243
Suspensions up thirty percent for Black
boys. The authors' own account says

39
00:02:11,243 --> 00:02:15,696
something narrower. In-school suspensions,
for Black students. And for out-of-school

40
00:02:15,696 --> 00:02:20,149
suspensions — the ones that remove a child
from the building — no significant effect

41
00:02:20,149 --> 00:02:20,520
at all.

42
00:02:20,570 --> 00:02:24,876
The scope shrank too. This is one large
Florida district, comparing schools that

43
00:02:24,876 --> 00:02:29,451
used phones more against schools that used
them less. Not a statewide evaluation. The

44
00:02:29,451 --> 00:02:33,434
overall academic difference is about one
percentile point — and it was not

45
00:02:33,434 --> 00:02:37,794
significant for girls, or for elementary
students. So all groups benefited is not

46
00:02:37,794 --> 00:02:38,870
what the study says.

47
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:43,060
Next, the study the essay used as its
clincher. Free software, forty-six dollars

48
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:47,252
a student, all of it teacher training, and
it moved state maths scores. The audit

49
00:02:47,252 --> 00:02:51,134
read the cost report. The forty-six
dollars covers platform maintenance and

50
00:02:51,134 --> 00:02:55,171
implementation support as well. The
intervention was a package, and you cannot

51
00:02:55,171 --> 00:02:56,620
pull the training out of it.

52
00:02:56,670 --> 00:03:00,953
Then the equity statistic. More than half
of students without home Wi-Fi get online

53
00:03:00,953 --> 00:03:04,875
by phone. Pull the camera back and look at
the denominator. Out of a hundred

54
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:09,004
children, four are smartphone-only and
three have nothing. The fraction is real.

55
00:03:09,004 --> 00:03:12,410
But it is a fraction of seven, not a
fraction of the student body.

56
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:16,689
The essay's best line was that every one
of those laws leaves the exemption

57
00:03:16,689 --> 00:03:18,945
undefined and not one state fills it in.

58
00:03:18,945 --> 00:03:22,779
Texas has no general classroom
educational-use exception at all — it

59
00:03:22,779 --> 00:03:27,290
names disability plans, documented medical
need, and safety. New York does let a

60
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:31,801
school authorise a specific educational
purpose. The blank is real in places. It

61
00:03:31,801 --> 00:03:32,760
is not universal.

62
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:37,207
And the essay said no new law addressed
the enforcement problem that killed New

63
00:03:37,207 --> 00:03:41,661
York's first ban a decade ago. New York's
own statute does. It bars suspending a

64
00:03:41,661 --> 00:03:45,724
student purely for using a device, and it
requires the district to report

65
00:03:45,724 --> 00:03:50,400
enforcement by demographic group and file
a plan if the disparities are significant.

66
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:55,022
One more. The thirty-seventy rule — thirty
percent on hardware, seventy on people. It

67
00:03:55,022 --> 00:03:58,787
is a real recommendation from a real
brief. From two thousand and two.

68
00:03:58,787 --> 00:04:03,251
Twenty-four years before the sentence that
cites it, and about human infrastructure

69
00:04:03,251 --> 00:04:05,080
generally, not about an AI budget.

70
00:04:05,130 --> 00:04:07,812
Five corrections in, the obvious question.

71
00:04:07,812 --> 00:04:09,280
Is there anything left?

72
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:13,623
Yes. The core of it. Sixty studies with
causal designs, pooled: coaching moves

73
00:04:13,623 --> 00:04:18,136
what teachers do by about half a standard
deviation, and moves what students learn

74
00:04:18,136 --> 00:04:22,319
by about a fifth. That is a real effect
from a real synthesis, and it is the

75
00:04:22,319 --> 00:04:24,300
strongest brick in the essay's wall.

76
00:04:24,350 --> 00:04:26,491
But read the same paper for its warning.

77
00:04:26,491 --> 00:04:30,933
The effect is not a constant. Much of the
evidence sits in early literacy and small

78
00:04:30,933 --> 00:04:35,482
trials — and as the programmes get bigger,
the effect gets smaller. Whatever coaching

79
00:04:35,482 --> 00:04:39,550
does, it does less of it at the scale a
district would actually have to buy.

80
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:43,636
And here is the study that should stop
anyone from saying more training, and

81
00:04:43,636 --> 00:04:47,671
stopping there. Around two hundred
fourth-grade teachers. Ninety-three hours

82
00:04:47,671 --> 00:04:49,530
of maths professional development —

83
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:53,566
content, collaboration, individual
feedback. Teacher knowledge went up. Some

84
00:04:53,566 --> 00:04:56,380
practices improved. Student achievement
did not move.

85
00:04:56,430 --> 00:05:00,752
So the honest version of the ASSISTments
result is not the training did it. It is

86
00:05:00,752 --> 00:05:05,022
that a package — software, training, a
warm-up year, and ongoing support — moved

87
00:05:05,022 --> 00:05:08,917
eighth-grade maths by a tenth of a
standard deviation for about forty-six

88
00:05:08,917 --> 00:05:12,920
dollars a student. That is still a good
buy. It is just not an argument for

89
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:13,720
training alone.

90
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:17,699
There is one more piece of good news, and
it is newer. Give tutors live AI

91
00:05:17,699 --> 00:05:22,160
assistance during a session and mastery of
the lesson topic rises four points — nine

92
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:25,983
points for the students of the
lowest-rated tutors. The help lands where

93
00:05:25,983 --> 00:05:29,966
the expertise is thinnest. End-of-year
maths, though, showed no significant

94
00:05:29,966 --> 00:05:30,550
difference.

95
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:34,652
Notice what every surviving result has in
common. None of them is a study of

96
00:05:34,652 --> 00:05:38,865
training. They are studies of supported
implementation — the tool and the human

97
00:05:38,865 --> 00:05:42,651
capacity to use it, bought together,
evaluated together. That is a real

98
00:05:42,651 --> 00:05:46,170
finding. It is a different finding from
the one the essay claimed.

99
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:50,999
Which leaves the sentence the whole essay
is built on. And that one has a different

100
00:05:50,999 --> 00:05:51,460
problem.

101
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:56,168
The claim is that training teachers in AI
improves what students learn. Go looking

102
00:05:56,168 --> 00:06:00,428
for the experiment that shows it. Trials
of coaching — yes. Trials of maths

103
00:06:00,428 --> 00:06:04,689
training — yes. Trials of AI tools with
tutors — yes. Trials of AI-specific

104
00:06:04,689 --> 00:06:08,040
teacher training measured on student
outcomes. Almost none.

105
00:06:08,090 --> 00:06:11,940
Which changes what kind of sentence this
is. The essay wrote: this is not a

106
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:15,945
philosophical claim, it is what the
evidence shows. The audit's answer is that

107
00:06:15,945 --> 00:06:19,949
it is a defensible bet. Those are both
respectable things to publish. They are

108
00:06:19,949 --> 00:06:23,851
not the same thing, and the reader
deserves to know which one they are being

109
00:06:23,851 --> 00:06:24,210
handed.

110
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:28,590
The essay's closing analogy has the same
shape. Doctors have mandatory continuing

111
00:06:28,590 --> 00:06:32,706
education, so teachers should too — and
teaching has no such system. Illinois

112
00:06:32,706 --> 00:06:36,715
requires a hundred and twenty hours for
licence renewal. The infrastructure

113
00:06:36,715 --> 00:06:40,884
exists. The argument that it should be
better is a different argument from the

114
00:06:40,884 --> 00:06:41,900
one the essay made.

115
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:46,225
Even the survey the essay leans on says
more than it was asked to. Seventy percent

116
00:06:46,225 --> 00:06:50,240
of teachers not using AI say they lack the
knowledge and skills. Ask the same

117
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:54,568
teachers a different question — what stops
you doing professional learning at all —

118
00:06:54,568 --> 00:06:58,530
and two-thirds say other responsibilities,
three in five say scheduling. The

119
00:06:58,530 --> 00:07:00,720
knowledge gap is real. So is the calendar.

120
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:05,622
An audit that only subtracts is half an
audit. Here is the study that would settle

121
00:07:05,622 --> 00:07:05,800
it.

122
00:07:05,850 --> 00:07:10,147
Give every school the same tools and the
same basic orientation. Then randomise

123
00:07:10,147 --> 00:07:14,009
which schools also get coaching and
protected time to collaborate. That

124
00:07:14,009 --> 00:07:18,415
comparison isolates the thing actually in
dispute — not whether technology helps,

125
00:07:18,415 --> 00:07:21,950
but whether the support wrapped around it
is what earns the gain.

126
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:26,271
And measure six things, not one. Did
teachers improve. Did students learn. Did

127
00:07:26,271 --> 00:07:30,597
the learning last. Did the teacher's
judgement last once the AI was taken away.

128
00:07:30,597 --> 00:07:34,540
Was access equal. And could the school
actually afford to keep doing it.

129
00:07:34,590 --> 00:07:38,756
And name what would prove the thesis
wrong, because a claim that cannot lose is

130
00:07:38,756 --> 00:07:42,816
not a claim. Run that trial. If the
coached schools and the uncoached schools

131
00:07:42,816 --> 00:07:47,245
land on the same student results, then the
money belongs in the tools after all, and

132
00:07:47,245 --> 00:07:48,300
the essay was wrong.

133
00:07:48,350 --> 00:07:52,131
So the verdict. The recommendation
survives — invest in the capacity to use

134
00:07:52,131 --> 00:07:56,265
the tools, not just the tools. What did
not survive is the evidence base as it was

135
00:07:56,265 --> 00:08:00,096
described: a subgroup narrowed, a cost
attributed to the wrong ingredient, a

136
00:08:00,096 --> 00:08:03,776
universal claim that two statutes
disprove, a benchmark from two thousand

137
00:08:03,776 --> 00:08:07,809
and two, and a finding that turns out to
be a bet. The essay is better after the

138
00:08:07,809 --> 00:08:10,380
audit than before it. That is what an
audit is for.

139
00:08:10,430 --> 00:08:13,862
Your turn. Take something you have
published — a post, a memo, a proposal —

140
00:08:13,862 --> 00:08:15,739
and do not ask Claude whether it is good.

141
00:08:15,739 --> 00:08:17,340
Ask it to run an adversarial audit:

142
00:08:17,340 --> 00:08:20,864
decompose the argument into separate
claims, rule on each one, and find every

143
00:08:20,864 --> 00:08:24,388
number that does not mean what the
sentence says it means. Ask it to tell you

144
00:08:24,388 --> 00:08:27,958
which of your claims is a finding and
which is a bet. That is the whole method

145
00:08:27,958 --> 00:08:30,200
in this film, and it works on anything you
wrote.

146
00:08:30,250 --> 00:08:33,040
Train the Teacher. Liam, in for Bear.
